# Curated landmark laws, Supreme Court rulings and historical events that moved the tracked numbers.
# bucket: "lib" = expands federal spending / government's economic role / progressive taxation / looser money
#         "con" = cuts taxes or spending / limits government's economic role / tighter or "hard" money
#         "mix" = mixed or cross-cutting (e.g., tariffs, wartime finance, balanced tax-and-spend deals)
# pattern: how the vote split, when known ("Bipartisan", "Party-line", "Mostly one party")
# metrics: which tracked numbers the item most directly moved: debt, deficit, interest, minwage, gdp
# cat: tax | spend | budget | money | wage | war | crisis

